	(text_box "Barometer. It is needed for the CO2 sensor as an input. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.05 46.99 0)
		(size 21.59 8.89)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "365969cd-ff75-47c4-a058-6a9511e1c318")
	)
	(text_box "STCC4 CO₂ sensor. This is the reason the system runs at 2.7V instead of 2.0V.\n\nThe datasheet doesn't specify the peak current consumption, but it says 100µA on average when measuring every 10 seconds, and one measurement takes 500ms. So I guess the consumption during the measurement is 2mA. If true, it can be handled by the C_STORE buffer capacitor.\n\nSDA_C and SDL_C is a nested I²C bus for connecting an SHT4x temperature/humidity sensor. However, that data can be supplied externally, so we're taking it from the ENS210."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 40.64 0)
		(size 66.04 27.94)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67b19d6d-90bb-4b1f-bca3-886067c3ceb4")
	)
	(text_box "ENS210 temperature and humidity sensor. It is a bit cheaper and a bit more accurate than Sensiron's SHT4x so I chose this. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 74.93 46.99 0)
		(size 25.4 19.05)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7a5d5ec4-59aa-4b50-9a36-f9de17f1aefe")
	)
	(text_box "I put a 1k resistor because we have a really tight current consumption budget. I am not sure how bright this will be."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 116.84 0)
		(size 48.26 11.43)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7c0a6194-5ba9-4d49-8f2f-48b9dec88b2d")
	)
	(text_box "These two connectors are for the capacitive buttons, and they go to the front panel which can be easily swapped when you want a new button configuration."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 43.18 95.25 0)
		(size 48.26 11.43)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
